1
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:30,670
Young Gar, stop!

2
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,830
Stop! Stop!

3
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:52,940
Young Gar...

4
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,970
Otto, you idiot.

5
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:07,580
You went and did something 
crazy, didn't you?

6
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:10,690
I never knew he had it in 'im.

7
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:14,340
To add insult to injury, 
he even won Ram over...

8
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:16,590
And now I look like this!

9
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:18,110
Ram?

10
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:19,300
What happened to them?

11
00:01:19,610 --> 00:01:23,470
What you guys are plotting 
don't mean shit to me.

12
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:24,890
You didn't kill them, did you?

13
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:26,980
I told ya, it don't mean shit!

14
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:31,200
Move. I'm gonna smash up the entrance,

15
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,820
and put an end to all of this.

16
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:38,610
If you do that, the Sanctuary 
will be closed off forever.

17
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,030
Is that what you want?

18
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,660
Yes, it is.

19
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,540
Every other damn thing is the problem!

20
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:04,160
What're you tryin' to pull? Huh?!

21
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:09,060
Garfiel, what are you so afraid of?

22
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,360
You think... I'm afraid?

23
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:14,560
You are.

24
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:18,860
That's why you're shouting and trying 
to make yourself look bigger, isn't it?

25
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:19,820
What are you...

26
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:23,130
What the hell do you think 
you know about me?!

27
00:02:23,130 --> 00:02:24,180
I do know.

28
00:02:24,590 --> 00:02:29,420
Because... I've been afraid of 
many things throughout my life.

29
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:33,580
I lived in fear right up until today.

30
00:02:34,230 --> 00:02:37,330
I left all the bad things in 
Puck's hands so I could forget them,

31
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:38,950
but now I've finally remembered.

32
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,090
Shut up.

33
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:44,740
I still haven't figured out 
what it is I need to do.

34
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,860
I need to find what that is.

35
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,100
But...

36
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:51,360
Shut up! Get out!

37
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:54,340
Don't you... Don't you even dare...

38
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:58,420
But you've already found that something 
for yourself, haven't you?

39
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,220
I told you to shut your damn mouth!

40
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,700
You're just too half-assed, Garfiel.

41
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,480
It's true that Emilia failed the trial once.

42
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,450
I can't deny that she cried her eyes out

43
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:11,260
when it showed her a past she 
didn't want to see, either.

44
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:15,280
But Emilia will keep trying, over and over.

45
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:18,720
Unlike you, the guy who 
gave up and ran away.

46
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:22,570
Garfiel, do you have a grudge

47
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:24,750
against your mother who abandoned you?

48
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,370
Sorry, man.

49
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:31,710
We take off our shoes when 
visiting someone's home,

50
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:36,270
but it's the Natsuki family way to trample 
all over people's hearts with our shoes on.

51
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:41,120
Your mother left you and Frederica 
behind when she left the Sanctuary.

52
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,120
And then... what did you do?

53
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,700
Frederica left the Sanctuary, too.

54
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:53,670
She believed you'd eventually liberate it,

55
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:57,770
so she left to make a place in the outside 
world for the people living here.

56
00:03:58,270 --> 00:04:01,300
And what have you been 
doing here on the inside?

57
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:06,460
You want to keep the Sanctuary closed 
off because you hate your mother

58
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:09,410
and the outside world 
that made her leave you?

59
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:11,250
Because you don't want to be hurt here?!

60
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:13,810
No, you're... What the hell do you...

61
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:15,970
I don't! Not unless you tell me!

62
00:04:15,970 --> 00:04:18,360
I won't understand until you speak!

63
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,740
If you hate your mother,

64
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:23,980
then bust out of here right now to 
get revenge on her or whatever!

65
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:26,910
Don't take it out on the rest of us in here!

66
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:31,130
You hate your family! If you didn't—

67
00:04:31,130 --> 00:04:31,790
You're wrong!

68
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:37,000
I... I...

69
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,190
Tell me the truth!

70
00:04:41,650 --> 00:04:45,020
I... wanted...

71
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:50,110
my mom to... be happy.

72
00:04:52,210 --> 00:04:54,080
We were in the way, weren't we?

73
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:58,550
My sister and I were in the way 
of her happiness, weren't we?!

74
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:01,430
It only makes sense!

75
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:03,790
She couldn't even stand to look at us!

76
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:07,870
If you're carryin' baggage like that, 
what's wrong with dumpin' it somewhere?!

77
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:12,210
Mom left so she could find happiness!

78
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,220
So I'm not holdin' anything against her!

79
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,180
But... I saw it.

80
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,090
I saw it in the graveyard...

81
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:25,740
Right after Mom left here, 
there was a landslide.

82
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:30,390
And she died!

83
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:37,850
Why? Didn't she leave here 
so she could find happiness?

84
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:45,150
Didn't she leave us behind so 
she could find happiness?!

85
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:51,840
If she abandoned us only to die 
before she could find happiness...

86
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,950
What are we supposed to do?

87
00:05:56,700 --> 00:06:00,440
I wanted Mom to be happy.

88
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:03,390
I wanted her to make me believe 
our sadness and loneliness

89
00:06:03,390 --> 00:06:08,570
served the purpose of helping 
her find happiness!

90
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:14,430
I wanted her to make me hate her!

91
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:21,400
I'm not lettin' you get 
to the outside world.

92
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:25,820
Things changing ain't gonna 
make everyone happy.

93
00:06:26,170 --> 00:06:29,360
For a lot of us, 
nothing's ever gonna get better!

94
00:06:31,170 --> 00:06:33,340
I'm gonna protect them.

95
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:38,620
I'm gonna protect everything 
and everyone within my reach.

96
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:41,890
I will become a barrier!

97
00:06:41,890 --> 00:06:46,000
A real barrier that separates 
the inside from the outside!

98
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,090
Garfiel!

99
00:06:47,090 --> 00:06:51,980
The Sanctuary, the people here, 
the old hag... I'll protect them all!

100
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:54,330
No one can do it but me!

101
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:56,450
No one will know but me!

102
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:59,440
And no one else <i>needs</i> to know!

103
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,200
Subaru!

104
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,410
It's okay, Emilia.

105
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:22,250
You're so damn stubborn.

106
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:25,860
I guess I'll have to force you into 
total submission to make you realize...

107
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:29,510
that you're just a big, sweet idiot!

108
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:34,600
You'd better survive this, body!

109
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:37,600
Shamac!

110
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,320
Thanks.

111
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:59,660
Come on down to my level, Garfiel!

112
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:23,870
Wh-What just...

113
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:32,570
Is this... my sister's?

114
00:08:33,070 --> 00:08:35,190
Damn it, why...

115
00:08:36,050 --> 00:08:37,630
Good question.

116
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:41,730
Maybe there's a really hungry 
cat hanging out inside it?

117
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,960
That's all the help I can give you.

118
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:46,810
Apparently, even when you can't talk,

119
00:08:46,810 --> 00:08:49,040
you find a way to be annoying by glowing.

120
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,510
Look at me, Garfiel.

121
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,770
Huh?

122
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:57,720
If you want to stop me, 
do it with your own hands.

123
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:02,370
Don't wuss out and hide behind 
your blood, you spineless coward!

124
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:05,630
When are you gonna stop 
taking me for a fool?

125
00:09:06,410 --> 00:09:08,790
We're going to the outside world.

126
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:10,610
Emilia will take on the graveyard.

127
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,190
The Sanctuary will be liberated.

128
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:14,310
Whether you want it or not.

129
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:17,160
Who asked you to do that?!

130
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,090
Who said you could?!

131
00:09:19,090 --> 00:09:21,980
This place doesn't need to change!

132
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:24,960
You know it's not gonna 
stay like this forever!

133
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:27,170
In the same way we've all 
been completely cornered,

134
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:30,740
there's gonna be a time when 
you'll be helpless on your own!

135
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,790
It could be tomorrow... or right now!

136
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,420
Just go down, Garfiel.

137
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:38,260
Learn what strength in numbers means!

138
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:40,730
There had to be...

139
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:43,770
a better way for you to say that!

140
00:10:02,850 --> 00:10:05,000
Take a good look, Garfiel.

141
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:08,960
The wall you're so afraid of doesn't exist.

142
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:13,330
It does exist! I am the wall!

143
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:17,580
I stopped here, and so did the 
old hag and everyone else.

144
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:19,200
And that's the end of it!

145
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,560
That means it's over!

146
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:22,980
Don't just give up on yourself!

147
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:26,520
Whenever you think, "I wanna 
do it! I wanna change!"

148
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:29,140
That's where your starting line is!

149
00:10:29,990 --> 00:10:32,270
When you decide to lift 
your head and walk again,

150
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:35,110
who has the right to stop you,
 for any reason?!

151
00:10:36,570 --> 00:10:39,280
Isn't that right, Garfiel?!

152
00:10:40,070 --> 00:10:42,640
Isn't that right, Emilia?!

153
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:45,080
And...

154
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:49,180
Isn't that right, Rem?!

155
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:54,320
Damn you!

156
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:37,990
Talk about a bad first impression 
for a new technique.

157
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,300
Come on, you've gotta be kidding.

158
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:48,440
Just how tough are you, man?

159
00:11:49,170 --> 00:11:52,270
Don't you... underestimate me.

160
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:56,830
As long as... I don't break...
 I can still...

161
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:01,040
Well, damn.

162
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:04,660
After all this, I have no choice 
but to recognize your strength.

163
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:08,500
This is... the end of it!

164
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,790
No one else will ever—

165
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,960
What do you think, Garfiel?

166
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,490
This is what you call "strength in numbers."

167
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:40,530
Again... there had to be...

168
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:44,280
a better way... to say that.

169
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,950
Okay, then. All of our 
feelings came together,

170
00:12:47,950 --> 00:12:49,910
and our bond won us this battle.

171
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:58,380
I guess nobody can lift 
a quain stone alone...

172
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:03,850
You finally said something that 
sounds like it came from you...

173
00:13:11,170 --> 00:13:14,810
<i>That nasty witch was probably behind it.</i>

174
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,770
<i>That Sloth Witch Factor 
that she talked about...</i>

175
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:20,320
Rawr!

176
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,150
<i>Unseen Hand... Unperceived Impact...</i>

177
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:28,820
<i>No... it's the invisible will of God.</i>

178
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:33,410
Invisible Providence. 
That's what I'll call it.

179
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:35,550
Huh? What did you say?

180
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:37,360
Uh, nothing.

181
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:44,270
You're letting me use your 
lap as a pillow again.

182
00:13:45,070 --> 00:13:48,170
I guess that's my reward for 
overcoming my biggest battle yet.

183
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:50,760
Yes, yes.

184
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,940
Oh, Natsuki-san, you're awa—

185
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:06,220
Wh-What did you do that for?!

186
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:08,130
Shut up, you idiot! You jerk!

187
00:14:08,130 --> 00:14:10,640
This happened because you went 
off and did your own thing!

188
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:14,080
But I guess I might have been 
in trouble without your help,

189
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:16,000
so it's not like I'm not grateful at all.

190
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,840
I don't know what you're talking about!

191
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:25,260
I'm glad you're all right.

192
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:31,500
Same to you, Natsuki-san.

193
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,950
Need a translation?

194
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:42,790
She said, "Don't worry me like that," right?

195
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:47,070
Also, "Don't get too full of yourself. 
There won't be a next time."

196
00:14:47,070 --> 00:14:49,520
That's where the extra rage is coming from.

197
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:52,780
Thanks, girl.

198
00:14:58,170 --> 00:15:00,520
So... where's Garfiel?

199
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:02,100
Over there.

200
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:06,620
But... I don't think we 
should interrupt just yet.

201
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,320
Interrupt?

202
00:15:09,650 --> 00:15:10,190
Yes.

203
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:17,930
Garf, you're awake?

204
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:21,360
Yeah... I'm awake.

205
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,930
Then get off me already.

206
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:27,190
My feet are going numb.

207
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:34,480
Still ain't a shred of 
niceness in you, is there?

208
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:37,970
When there's someone worth being 
nice to, I can be nice.

209
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:38,560
Wha...

210
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:43,080
And I'm not worth that, huh?

211
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,270
Sorry.

212
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:46,650
If you want to hear a lady's true feelings,

213
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:47,920
try a little harder.

214
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:55,380
Garf, you're too stupid.

215
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:56,850
It's no use trying to think.

216
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:57,390
Huh?

217
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:01,310
From now on, fight with an empty head 
and don't think about anything.

218
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:04,230
For myself, and for Emilia-sama, too.

219
00:16:05,290 --> 00:16:05,980
Buh—

220
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:07,950
Don't be dumb!

221
00:16:07,950 --> 00:16:09,800
I admit that I lost!

222
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:13,760
But admitting and surrendering 
are two different things!

223
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:15,570
I could pick up where I left off right—

224
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:16,570
Stop yammering!

225
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:21,950
You lost, Garf, you purrfect loser.

226
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:26,840
How long must you carry on in front of the 
woman you love before you're satisfied?

227
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:32,610
S-So you want me to just fall in line 
beside the rest of you with a smile?

228
00:16:32,610 --> 00:16:36,850
I accept that I lost, but I 
don't accept that I was wrong!

229
00:16:36,850 --> 00:16:41,190
That's right! I don't 
think I was in the wrong!

230
00:16:41,190 --> 00:16:43,520
So I can't make some 
half-assed attempt to—

231
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:45,650
If you don't want it to stop at half-assed,

232
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:48,420
you just need to prove that 
you're not standing still.

233
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:49,160
Huh?

234
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,430
The trial...

235
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:56,970
Can you change,

236
00:16:56,970 --> 00:17:00,810
or are you going to be a little cowering 
child stuck in one place forever?

237
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:03,470
Find out with your own eyes.

238
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:07,840
Don't say it in a way that 
makes me wanna deny it!

239
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,170
Don't just give up on yourself!

240
00:17:17,990 --> 00:17:20,740
You look as if you've made up your mind.

241
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:23,840
You'll be fine, Garf.

242
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:28,600
If anything frightens you to the 
point of tears, I'll comfort you.

243
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:31,040
As a favor to an old friend, you know?

244
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:51,760
Damn it all!

245
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:02,860
<i>First, you must confront your own past.</i>

246
00:18:28,490 --> 00:18:30,480
Mom...

247
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:34,800
You insist on going?

248
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:35,820
Yes.

249
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:40,080
Although I know it will 
impose a burden on you...

250
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:43,360
I am not concerned with that.

251
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:45,270
The greater issue is...

252
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:48,140
how these two little ones feel.

253
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:55,190
You piece of shit!

254
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:02,010
Mother, I-I...

255
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,770
I'm sorry, Fred, dear.

256
00:19:06,130 --> 00:19:09,540
I know this is causing so 
much worry for you, too.

257
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:15,040
I'm all right... but I feel bad for Garf.

258
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:19,510
I wish we could go together, 
but I'm just so clumsy.

259
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:23,300
I know it would be an 
awful experience for him.

260
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:27,780
Fred, you're very responsible, 
even for a child of mine,

261
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:28,890
so please take care of him.

262
00:19:30,110 --> 00:19:32,350
No! Don't!

263
00:19:32,350 --> 00:19:35,020
Mom, don't go outside!

264
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:36,510
Here.

265
00:19:38,450 --> 00:19:40,750
For you and Gar.

266
00:19:46,190 --> 00:19:47,120
Gar, sweetie,

267
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,710
your mommy has to go now.

268
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,830
Don't!

269
00:19:57,210 --> 00:20:01,310
I promise I'll bring your father back.

270
00:20:01,650 --> 00:20:03,820
Just wait until then.

271
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:08,850
My... father?

272
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:15,190
That's a lie... That's wrong.

273
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:19,630
You left here to find happiness.

274
00:20:19,630 --> 00:20:25,660
Mother loved both you and me dearly, Garf.

275
00:20:26,260 --> 00:20:29,820
She left the Sanctuary 
for her family's sake.

276
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:32,980
Are you not content with that?

277
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:37,020
L-Like hell she did! 
If she loved us, then why—

278
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:40,420
It probably made things easier
believing that she didn't love us.

279
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:44,410
If you believed that your love was one-sided,

280
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:46,750
you could justify the pain it caused you.

281
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:48,960
No! You're wrong!

282
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,430
You don't know anything!

283
00:20:50,430 --> 00:20:52,290
When Mom leaves here, she's gonna—

284
00:20:52,290 --> 00:20:54,320
Of course I know that.

285
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:54,880
Huh?

286
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:56,650
There's no way I wouldn't.

287
00:20:57,330 --> 00:21:02,190
If Mother did meet misfortune 
upon leaving here,

288
00:21:02,190 --> 00:21:05,450
do you think Grandmother 
would not inform us?

289
00:21:05,450 --> 00:21:08,320
Then... Then why?!

290
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:12,240
You must know why you were not 
told at such a young age.

291
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:17,560
Because, Garf, you are 
no longer a young child.

292
00:21:20,830 --> 00:21:25,290
In truth, you remembered that 
Mother loved you, didn't you?

293
00:21:26,290 --> 00:21:30,470
You have that scar on your forehead 
because you wanted to forget her kiss.

294
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:33,960
You wanted to make it disappear, 
so you gave it to yourself.

295
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,980
This is the end of your past.

296
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:45,450
Wait...

297
00:21:45,770 --> 00:21:46,700
Wait a minute!

298
00:21:47,370 --> 00:21:49,570
What am I supposed to do?

299
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:53,560
If you must rely on your older sister 
even when she's still so young,

300
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:55,250
you will never find your answer.

301
00:21:55,610 --> 00:21:57,600
I know it's pathetic!

302
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,200
But you're the only one I can count on!

303
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,000
Please...

304
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:04,960
What do you want to do, Garf?

305
00:22:08,690 --> 00:22:12,140
What do you want to do, Garf?

306
00:22:14,790 --> 00:22:17,470
I wanna do what I'm expected to do.

307
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:21,040
What who expects you to do?

308
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:25,740
The people... All the people who need me.

309
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,030
I wanna do what they expect me to.

310
00:22:28,530 --> 00:22:31,990
And what makes you feel that way?

311
00:22:36,710 --> 00:22:40,310
They made me remember...

312
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,630
that Mom...

313
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:49,190
really loved me.

314
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:05,610
So... Is Shima-san Ryuzu-san's older 
sister, or her younger sister?

315
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:10,430
Uh, actually... that's kinda confusing, 
so we'll save it for later.

316
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:15,220
Young Gar!

317
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,840
Y-Young Gar...

318
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:21,290
You see, I... We...

319
00:23:21,770 --> 00:23:24,670
Don't make that face, old hags.
 It don't suit ya.

320
00:23:27,730 --> 00:23:30,110
Sorry I worried you.

321
00:23:34,850 --> 00:23:36,870
Garf, how did it go?

322
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:42,310
Well, I can't say I really got any 
results you can see out of it.

323
00:23:42,690 --> 00:23:46,770
But... I do think I got some closure.

324
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,740
Okay, then, let's do the 
rest of the trial while—

325
00:23:52,740 --> 00:23:55,270
Now, that ain't my job.

326
00:23:55,270 --> 00:23:58,050
That's right. It's my job.

327
00:23:58,050 --> 00:24:00,020
Don't just go and take it.

328
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:01,280
Yeah, uh...

329
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,200
I also wanna say...

330
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:07,300
I think the reason I finally 
accepted the trial

331
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:09,490
was probably because of you.

332
00:24:10,330 --> 00:24:11,240
Thanks.

333
00:24:13,700 --> 00:24:15,640
Did you just say "thanks"?

334
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:17,400
I'm not gonna say it again!

335
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:18,060
Listen up!

336
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,320
I realize I lost!

337
00:24:20,320 --> 00:24:25,740
But if you guys liberate this place and the 
old hags suffer for it, I won't go easy on ya!

338
00:24:25,740 --> 00:24:27,770
Y-Yeah, of course...

339
00:24:27,770 --> 00:24:32,280
Which means I'm gonna be here to 
make sure you're not all talk!

340
00:24:32,790 --> 00:24:35,960
So make sure ya do it right, boss!

341
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:36,320
Ow!

342
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,050
His face was so red!

343
00:24:40,050 --> 00:24:41,860
Boss?

344
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:44,790
Between the two of us, 
you're above me, though.

345
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:47,790
I bet you feel as if you've 
gained a new brother.

346
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:50,550
You're older than he is, so be lenient.

347
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:52,820
Well, in that case...

348
00:24:52,820 --> 00:24:54,250
Wait a minute!

349
00:24:54,250 --> 00:24:57,510
Did you just say he's younger than me?!

350
00:24:58,750 --> 00:25:01,220
Garf is only turning fourteen this year.

351
00:25:03,650 --> 00:25:06,650
He's an eighth grader!

352
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:14,660
Are you going?

353
00:25:15,660 --> 00:25:20,260
Yeah. If I stay here too long,
 my resolve will waver.

354
00:25:22,610 --> 00:25:23,620
Hey, Subaru...

355
00:25:25,430 --> 00:25:28,240
About what happened in the graveyard...

356
00:25:31,730 --> 00:25:32,740
Emilia?

357
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:35,760
Y-You know! When we...

358
00:25:39,090 --> 00:25:41,580
Um... it means a lot to me,

359
00:25:41,580 --> 00:25:44,660
so when the trial and everything 
else is taken care of,

360
00:25:44,660 --> 00:25:46,340
let's talk it over... okay?

361
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:47,230
Uh-huh! Uh-huh!

362
00:25:51,930 --> 00:25:54,900
Talking now about what you'll 
do when it's over...

363
00:25:54,900 --> 00:25:57,410
You must be pretty confident, Emilia-tan.

364
00:25:57,730 --> 00:25:58,860
I'm not sure.

365
00:25:59,300 --> 00:26:02,240
Maybe I'm just putting up a tough front.

366
00:26:03,380 --> 00:26:05,040
I know it'll work out.

367
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:09,310
I'll wager a date with you on that!

368
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:12,100
Yes, of course.

369
00:26:16,260 --> 00:26:18,560
I'll be going now.

370
00:26:18,560 --> 00:26:19,900
Go get 'em!

371
00:26:19,900 --> 00:26:22,390
Watch out for cars and boys!

372
00:26:23,150 --> 00:26:24,640
Don't be silly.

373
00:26:32,370 --> 00:26:34,560
A giltylaw that came one step short?

374
00:26:35,140 --> 00:26:38,640
Ya can't be much of a man if ya 
keep lookin' all worried, boss.

375
00:26:39,110 --> 00:26:43,300
The way you talk makes sense now that 
I know you're an eighth grader.

376
00:26:43,300 --> 00:26:46,370
I rattled off a lot of quotes from famous 
people when I was that age, too.

377
00:26:46,370 --> 00:26:51,960
Hey, listen... There's somethin' 
I oughta apologize to you for.

378
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:54,340
Well, that's admirable of you.

379
00:26:54,340 --> 00:26:57,070
Go on, then. You can talk to 
your boss about anything.

380
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,840
Man, I'm embarrassed just saying that.

381
00:27:00,570 --> 00:27:02,900
I saw you.

382
00:27:03,340 --> 00:27:04,000
Huh?

383
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:06,870
When you, uh... you know...

384
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:09,720
got a little... desperate?

385
00:27:13,540 --> 00:27:16,570
What? O-Oh, crap! I forgot!

386
00:27:16,570 --> 00:27:20,040
But I mean, I wasn't 
expecting you to come in!

387
00:27:20,490 --> 00:27:22,570
But seeing that made me realize somethin'.

388
00:27:22,570 --> 00:27:25,840
You may be a complete dumbass,

389
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:29,390
but I'm sure glad you're the one I lost to!

390
00:27:29,390 --> 00:27:31,390
Shut up! Just forget about it!

391
00:27:31,390 --> 00:27:33,680
You're not a kid, so 
pretend you... didn't...

392
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:35,710
Wait, you <i>are</i> a kid!

393
00:27:41,450 --> 00:27:43,380
Subaru, you dummy.

394
00:27:49,850 --> 00:27:52,310
<i>"Give it your best. I know you can do it."</i>

395
00:27:52,830 --> 00:27:54,520
<i>"Puck and I are both rooting for you."</i>

396
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:57,020
<i>"When this is over, let's go on a date!"</i>

397
00:28:01,730 --> 00:28:03,960
You really are a dummy.

398
00:28:05,780 --> 00:28:07,340
Dummy... Dummy...

399
00:28:07,650 --> 00:28:09,380
Subaru, you nincompoop.

400
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:12,290
How could you break your 
promise to stay with me?

401
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:17,260
I swear, I'm never, ever going to 
forgive you until you apologize.

402
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:29,420
Hi there. I certainly have had 
a lot of visitors lately.

403
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:36,870
Awfully bold of you to stroll in here 
after that disgraceful display before.

404
00:28:36,870 --> 00:28:38,940
Even I'm surprised.

405
00:28:39,490 --> 00:28:41,680
You loose woman, who kisses up to

406
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:45,910
the first man to comfort you 
when you're sobbing in despair...

407
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:50,090
You shameless fool, who keeps soiling 
the world that is mine alone...

408
00:28:50,510 --> 00:28:55,340
You utterly selfish hedonist, 
who loves the you that he's forgiven...

409
00:28:56,580 --> 00:28:58,290
Well, why don't you say something...

410
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:00,630
witch's daughter?

411
00:29:06,610 --> 00:29:09,010
My name is simply Emilia!

412
00:29:09,380 --> 00:29:12,980
I am the Frozen Witch, born in Elior Forest!

413
00:29:18,300 --> 00:29:21,280
I won't give in to the 
malice of a fellow witch.

414
00:29:21,970 --> 00:29:24,820
I'm quite an insufferable woman, after all!

415
00:29:25,450 --> 00:29:29,950
Nobody Can Lift a Quain Stone Alone

416
00:29:34,820 --> 00:29:44,820


